      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Do not answer "should I do an MBA without work experience" in the abstract based on what one
    relative, one coaching institute, or one confident forum post told you.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      Build a real target list split into fresher-friendly institutes and experience-first
      institutes, using the data above, not a generic "top MBA colleges" ranking.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then take one honest, timed mock of your target entrance exam before spending a rupee on
      coaching, so the whole decision rests on a real number instead of a hopeful one.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Whether you go straight in or build a year or two of real work first, the decision that
    actually protects your income is not the MBA label by itself — it is pairing whichever path you
    choose with a genuine <strong>high-value skill portfolio</strong> the market can see and trust.
    Move toward that with
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    if you want a second opinion on your specific situation, or start with the free
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments">career and skill assessments</a>
    if you are still unsure whether a management path is genuinely your lane.
  </p>

